OMDb API supports parameters like:

apikey – Required (your API key)
t – Title (exact match)
s – Search term (partial match, returns multiple results)
i – IMDb ID
y – Year
plot – short or full
type – movie, series, or episode
page – Pagination (1–100)
Example 1 – Search by title keyword
Bash

Copy code
curl "http://www.omdbapi.com/?apikey=YOUR_API_KEY&s=batman&type=movie&page=1"
Explanation:

s=batman ? Search for movies containing “batman”
type=movie ? Only movies
page=1 ? First page of results
Example 2 – Get full details by exact title
Bash

Copy code
curl "http://www.omdbapi.com/?apikey=YOUR_API_KEY&t=Inception&y=2010&plot=full"
Explanation:

t=Inception ? Exact match title
y=2010 ? Year filter
plot=full ? Full plot instead of short
Example 3 – Get details by IMDb ID
Bash

Copy code
curl "http://www.omdbapi.com/?apikey=YOUR_API_KEY&i=tt1375666"
Explanation:

i=tt1375666 ? IMDb ID for Inception
